# Voice Modes - Three-Mode Voice System ✅

## Three Distinct Voice Interaction Modes

Juno implements **three completely separate voice interaction modes** that share the same voice transcription infrastructure but serve entirely different purposes and workflows.

## Mode Overview

| Mode | Trigger | Purpose | UI State | Processing | Memory |
|------|---------|---------|-----------|------------|---------|
| **Dictation Mode** | Hold configured key | Voice-to-text typing | Orange mic | Transcription only | None |
| **Agent Mode** | Alt+D toggle | AI conversations | Blue mic + chat | Full AI agent system | Persistent |
| **Always Listening** | Background continuous | Intent detection | Background indicator | Wake word detection | None |

## Dictation Mode

### Purpose
**Immediate voice-to-text typing** - replaces keyboard input for fast text entry.

### Activation
- **Trigger**: Configurable key (default: spacebar)
- **Behavior**: Hold key down to record, release to commit
- **UI State**: Orange microphone icon

### Workflow
```
Voice Input → Transcription → Text Insertion at Cursor Location
```

### Characteristics
- **No AI Processing**: Pure voice transcription service
- **Immediate Output**: Text appears at current cursor position
- **No Intelligence**: Direct speech-to-text conversion only
- **Use Case**: Replaces typing for emails, documents, code comments, etc.
- **Similar To**: Built-in macOS dictation feature

### Technical Implementation
- **Backend**: [src-tauri/src/spacebar_monitor.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/spacebar_monitor.rs)
- **Events**: `dictation-transcription-start`, `dictation-transcription-finish`
- **State**: `dictation_active` flag prevents AI processing
- **Timing**: 0ms start, 500ms commitment threshold

## Agent Mode

### Purpose
**AI agent conversations and task execution** - full Computer Use capabilities.

### Activation
- **Trigger**: Alt+D (Option+D on macOS)
- **Behavior**: Toggle to start/stop agent interaction
- **UI State**: Blue microphone icon, full chat interface

### Workflow
```
Voice Input → Transcription → AI Agent Processing → Agent Response/Actions
```

### Characteristics
- **Full AI Processing**: Hierarchical agent system with orchestrator and specialists
- **Computer Use Tools**: All 17 Anthropic actions (screenshot, mouse, keyboard, etc.)
- **Task Execution**: Can perform complex multi-step computer automation
- **Conversational**: Maintains conversation history and context
- **Use Case**: AI assistant for computer automation, coding, research, etc.

### Technical Implementation
- **Backend**: [src-tauri/src/anthropic.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/anthropic.rs) - Orchestrator agent
- **Events**: `app-dictation-started`, `app-dictation-finished`
- **Architecture**: Multi-agent system with browser, desktop, file specialists
- **Memory**: Persistent conversation history

## Always Listening Mode

### Purpose
**Continuous background monitoring** - detects wake words and user intent.

### Activation
- **Trigger**: Background continuous monitoring
- **Behavior**: Volume threshold detection → Wake word recognition → Agent activation
- **UI State**: Background indicator (no prominent mic icon)

### Workflow
```
Continuous Audio → Volume Detection → Wake Word Recognition → Agent Mode Activation
```

### Characteristics
- **Background Operation**: Non-intrusive continuous monitoring
- **Wake Word Detection**: Configurable phrases trigger activation (default: "hey juno", "computer")
- **Volume Threshold**: Sensitivity-based activation to prevent false positives
- **Intent Detection**: Bridges passive monitoring to active agent interaction
- **Use Case**: Hands-free activation, ambient computing, accessibility support

### Technical Implementation
- **Backend**: [tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/src/always_listening.rs](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/src/always_listening.rs)
- **Commands**: [src-tauri/src/commands/always_listening.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/commands/always_listening.rs)
- **Events**: `always_listening_started`, `always_listening_wake_word_detected`
- **Architecture**: Two-state system (Monitoring → Activated)
- **Configuration**: Adjustable sensitivity (0.1-2.0) and custom wake words

## Mode Coordination and Architecture

### Completely Separate Workflows
| Aspect | Dictation Mode | Agent Mode | Always Listening |
|--------|----------------|------------|------------------|
| **Purpose** | Voice typing replacement | AI conversation & automation | Intent detection |
| **Output** | Text at cursor | AI responses/actions | Agent mode activation |
| **Processing** | Transcription only | Full AI agent system | Wake word detection |
| **UI** | Orange mic | Blue mic + chat interface | Background indicator |
| **Memory** | None | Persistent conversation | None |
| **Tools** | None | All Computer Use tools | None |
| **State** | Temporary | Persistent | Background |

### Shared Infrastructure
- **Voice Transcription**: All modes use the same Whisper.cpp-based transcription engine
- **Audio Capture**: Same microphone input and processing pipeline
- **Plugin System**: All leverage [tauri-plugin-voice-transcription](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription)
- **Event System**: Common transcription events, different result handling

### State Management Coordination
```rust
// Backend coordination prevents conflicts
let is_dictation_active = app_state.dictation_active.lock()
    .map(|active| *active)
    .unwrap_or(false);

let is_always_listening_active = app_state.always_listening_active.lock()
    .map(|active| *active)
    .unwrap_or(false);

if is_dictation_active {
    // Route to immediate typing (Dictation Mode)
    return;
}

if is_always_listening_active && wake_word_detected {
    // Transition to Agent Mode
    activate_agent_mode();
    return;
}
// Route to AI agent (Agent Mode)
```

### Priority Handling
1. **Active Dictation**: Highest priority - pauses always listening, prevents agent activation
2. **Always Listening**: Background priority - continuous monitoring when not dictating
3. **Agent Mode**: On-demand priority - activated by Alt+D or wake word detection
4. **Wake Word Detection**: Seamlessly transitions always listening → agent mode

## Implementation Guidelines

### Terminology Standards
- **NEVER** use "spacebar mode" - always "Dictation Mode"
- **NEVER** use "option D mode" - always "Agent Mode"
- **NEVER** use "background mode" - always "Always Listening Mode"
- **ALWAYS** specify which mode when discussing voice features
- **REMEMBER**: Keyboard shortcuts are configurable, modes are functional

### UI State Management
```typescript
// Frontend state differentiation
const [isDictationMode, setIsDictationMode] = useState(false);
const [isAlwaysListening, setIsAlwaysListening] = useState(false);
const [barState, setBarState] = useState<BarState>("default");

// State mappings:
// "dictating" - Orange microphone (Dictation Mode)
// "listening" - Blue microphone (Agent Mode)
// "always_listening" - Background indicator (Always Listening Mode)
```

### Event Handling Coordination
```typescript
// Dictation Mode events
unlistenDictationStart = await listen("dictation-transcription-start", () => {
    setIsDictationMode(true);
    setBarState("dictating");
});

// Agent Mode events
unlistenAgentStart = await listen("app-dictation-started", () => {
    setIsDictationMode(false);
    setBarState("listening");
});

// Always Listening events
unlistenAlwaysListeningStart = await listen("always_listening_started", () => {
    setIsAlwaysListening(true);
});

unlistenWakeWordDetected = await listen("always_listening_wake_word_detected", () => {
    // Transition to Agent Mode
    setBarState("listening");
});
```

### Mode Interaction Patterns

#### Wake Word → Agent Transition
```typescript
// Always listening detects wake word and seamlessly activates agent
const handleWakeWordDetected = async () => {
    // Always listening automatically transitions to agent mode
    // No user intervention required
    setBarState("listening");
    // Agent conversation can begin immediately
};
```

#### Dictation Override
```typescript
// Dictation mode temporarily pauses always listening
const handleDictationStart = async () => {
    // Always listening automatically pauses
    setIsDictationMode(true);
    setBarState("dictating");
    // Always listening resumes after dictation completes
};
```

## Configuration and Settings

### Always Listening Configuration
- **Sensitivity**: 0.1 (quiet) to 2.0 (sensitive) - balances detection vs false positives
- **Wake Words**: Configurable array, default: `["hey juno", "computer"]`
- **Silence Timeout**: 3 seconds before returning to monitoring state
- **Background Operation**: Can run continuously without UI prominence

### Dictation Configuration
- **Activation Key**: Configurable (default: spacebar)
- **Commitment Threshold**: 500ms hold time before activation
- **Instant Start**: 0ms delay for immediate transcription

### Agent Configuration
- **Toggle Key**: Alt+D (Option+D on macOS)
- **Conversation History**: Persistent across sessions
- **Tool Access**: Full Computer Use API capabilities

## User Documentation Pattern

When documenting voice features:

✅ **CORRECT**:
- "Dictation Mode (default spacebar) for voice typing"
- "Agent Mode (Alt+D) for AI conversations"
- "Always Listening Mode for wake word detection"
- "Three-mode voice system with coordinated operation"

❌ **INCORRECT**:
- "Spacebar mode", "Option D toggle", "Background mode"
- "Two-mode system" (outdated)

This ensures documentation remains accurate even if keyboard shortcuts change in the future and properly reflects the complete three-mode architecture.
